course: dictionary
lesson: 12828
title: Employed: a job, a payment, or a method
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word employed has three meanings, and the words around it tell you which one. Read the context first. «Mum is employed as a nurse at the hospital.» Here employed means she has a paid job.
explain: «The shop employed eight workers last summer.» Now employed means the shop gave those people jobs and paid them. Ask yourself: who is giving the work?
explain: «The scientists chose a careful method and employed it in every test.» Here employed means used. In exam questions you may read «the method employed», which just means the method that was used.
fact: Employed means having a paid job, or giving someone a paid job.
fact: Employed can also mean used, especially in formal writing: «the method employed».
fact: Employ is the base word; employs, employed and employing are its other forms.
fact: Self-employed means working for yourself, not for an employer.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in "had a job", "gave a job" or "used" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «My aunt is employed by a bank in the city.» What does employed mean here? | Lost in the city | Tired and hungry | *Having a paid job | Used for a test
exercise: «The farmer employed three helpers to pick the apples.» What does employed mean here? | Used three apples | Found three lost apples | Hid from the helpers | *Gave three people paid work
exercise: In «The method employed by the team was clever», which word is the past form of employ? | method | clever | *employed | team
test: «Dad is self-employed, so he works for himself.» What does self-employed mean? | Is very busy at home | Is always on holiday | *Works for himself, not for an employer | Has a job at a school
test: «The method employed in the experiment was careful.» What does employed mean here? | Hidden | Lost | Paid | *Used
exam: Sam reads: «The company employed 50 people, so it paid 50 workers.» Which meaning of employed fits best? | Used a method | Was very hungry | *Gave people paid jobs | Lost its way
